WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.610
Most of your emails are never even seen.

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.110
They're sitting in spam, or
in a folder nobody checks.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.130
Here's why that happens,
and what to fix first.

4
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.580
Every email gets scored in real
time by the receiving server,

5
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.710
before a human ever sees it.

6
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.160
Four things drive that score.

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.100
Your domain reputation.

8
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.340
A new domain with no sending history
gets no benefit of the doubt.

9
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.110
Your sending pattern.

10
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:31.030
Jumping from five emails a day to five
hundred overnight looks like a spam

11
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.780
campaign, because it usually is one.

12
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.660
Your content. Spammy
language, too many links,

13
00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.710
and identical copy sent
to hundreds of people.

14
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.340
And your engagement.

15
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.840
When people don't open, don't
reply, or mark you as spam,

16
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.950
providers learn from it, and route
your future mail straight to junk.

17
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.390
No platform, including ours, can guarantee
the inbox if the basics aren't in

18
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.330
place. Two things are on you.

19
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.320
One: warm up your domain,
in both directions.

20
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.210
Outgoing: email people you actually
know and ask them to reply.

21
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:12.480
If you land in spam, ask
them to mark it 'not spam'.

22
00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.990
That's one of the strongest
trust signals you can generate.

23
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.980
Spread those asks over a few days.

24
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.720
Replies clustered in the
same hour look coordinated.

25
00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:27.000
Incoming: subscribe to a few
newsletters and open them.

26
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.620
An inbox that only sends and
never receives looks synthetic.

27
00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.290
Then ease into volume
over two to three weeks.

28
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.580
Two: clean your list.

29
00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.690
Bounces are one of the fastest ways
to burn the reputation you just built.

30
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.150
And the fix most people get
stuck on?

31
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:54.550
Think of inbox placement
as a stack of odds.

32
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.970
Every step in RepMail removes
one more reason to get flagged.

33
00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:04.510
Upload your list. RepMail reads
your CSV or Excel file and maps

34
00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.990
columns into variables
like name and company.

35
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.530
Build the template.

36
00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.690
Write it yourself,
or let the AI write it.

37
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.700
Preview every email.

38
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.840
Run the spam check,

39
00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:22.230
and anything flagged gets
fixed by AI in one click.

40
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.450
Then confirm. See every send
detail, credits included,

41
00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.770
before anything goes out.

42
00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.030
Warm up properly and keep your list clean.
That's on you.

43
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.670
Everything else, writing,
personalization,

44
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:42.010
spam checks, authentication and
sending, RepMail takes off your plate.

45
00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.450
So landing in the inbox
stops being a guessing game.

46
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.900
Get started with RepMail below.
